TEXT -384 56 Left 2 ;In the 3 phase case  the inductances of \nthe phases differs because of the\ndifferent coupling values of the \nphases.\nfor the inductive coupling matrix \nsee also Oil_400kV_Cable.txt
TEXT 280 -160 Left 2 ;Resistor of primary circuit = 0.18 ohm\nResistor of shield circuit added
TEXT -456 136 Left 2 ;Note: The shield current is dependent of some parameters: \n1) The thickness of the shield\n2) The placement of the conductors \n3) Solid or not solid shield\nThe ATP file from the examples in this folder is with \nSolid thick shield with (conductor 1m distance) and in this special\ndemonstrating case with coupling factor 1  so the shielding is perfect\nThis is not true in real world case so the shield current will be\nnormally much smaller then the conductor current especially\nif the shield is crossbonded
